1
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,880
kicking a pebble,
I leap off with a bear's stride,

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to Kashiwa, the type who was out jogging,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that I'd stay
just as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up my energy again,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,700
with guts, there's a reason to try.

7
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,020
One nightmare after another,
nothing changes.

8
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,880
The town's streetscape is kinder somehow.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:47,020
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,720
the sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,860
Can you really see the yakitori?

12
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:57,500
Of the pointed hat,

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:04,060
the sunset falls from the
people to the great one.

14
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too,
you'll drop it and it'll all end, won't it?

15
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,740
Magazine or not,
even the happiness we laughed at,

16
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:16,300
because I'm a fool who only
realized it after losing it.

17
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:26,680
Senpai, look at this.

18
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,980
I found it at the back of a drawer.

19
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,340
It's Ibu-chan's wedding photo, isn't it?

20
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:35,080
You look like a father
sending off his only daughter.

21
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,240
Honda made such a fuss, it was quite a job.

22
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,980
They're such close siblings, after all.

23
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:42,920
Since it was a student marriage,
I was worried.

24
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:45,820
But both Ibu-chan and her husband,
Kawasaki-kun,

25
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,540
will be graduating soon, won't they?

26
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:49,740
I wonder where they'll end up working.

27
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:50,660
I see.

28
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:55,040
Long time no see, everyone.

29
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,120
Hello.

30
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,780
Kawasaki-kun,

31
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,760
Ibu-chan.

32
00:01:58,760 --> 00:01:59,720
It's been a while.

33
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:03,080
Thank you so much for
everything when we got married.

34
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,840
We were just talking about you two.

35
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:08,040
Wondering where you'd end up working.

36
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:12,260
Actually, about that job,

37
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,020
we wanted to ask all of you for advice.

38
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:15,420
What is it?

39
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,640
So that's the situation.

40
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,780
You two are impressive.

41
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,300
We haven't told our families yet,

42
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:25,780
and we're struggling with how
to tell my brother in particular.

43
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:27,740
That's a big problem, isn't it?

44
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,700
Don't worry.

45
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:32,080
I'll tell Honda for you.

46
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,440
You're going to do it, Senpai?

47
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:37,020
I know Honda's personality inside and out.

48
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:40,020
I also know the method
that causes the least shock.

49
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:43,040
Even though that method
failed us when we got married.

50
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:48,120
This time it'll be fine!
Leave everything to me!

51
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:50,780
P-please, we're counting on you!

52
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,040
Come on, the whole Honda family!

53
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,460
Ryuzo-dono!

54
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:05,720
What is it? Suddenly saying
you have something to talk about.

55
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:06,920
Ryo-chan's in the back.

56
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:07,600
I see.

57
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,140
You came, Honda.

58
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,580
What is it? What did you want to talk about?

59
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:15,900
Well, it's like this.

60
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:18,120
Ibu had her baby!

61
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,800
Ibu had a baby...

62
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,040
What nonsense are you talking about, senpai?

63
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,300
Ibu hasn't had any kids yet.

64
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,760
I mean the game, the game.

65
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:29,640
The game.

66
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:32,860
It's a pretty interesting simulation game,
you know.

67
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,920
It's like watching a whole life play out.

68
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,640
Simulation game.

69
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:41,080
Right. So, the character I'm
raising in the game is named Eve.

70
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:43,580
Eve's child was a boy, right?

71
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,820
But I wanted to give it the
same name as my little sister.

72
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:50,480
Naming it after someone you know makes you feel closer to it,
doesn't it?

73
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:51,880
But it's better, you know.

74
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,220
What's the problem? It's just a game.

75
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:58,060
Can we really leave
everything to Ryo-chan alone?

76
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,220
I'm worried.

77
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,260
So, what is it?
What did you want to talk about?

78
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:02,840
Well, about that.

79
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:07,700
Oh no! Eve has to move far away
because her husband got transferred!

80
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,360
Waaaaah!

81
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:12,440
Now Eve has to leave her hometown too!

82
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,280
Mohahaha

83
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,040
Iimo

84
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,900
Senpai, are you okay?

85
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:21,580
Don't cry just because
Ibu is going far away, okay?

86
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:23,400
Iimo

87
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,120
What's wrong?

88
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:28,200
What do you mean, "what's wrong"?

89
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:32,060
It's just a game, and Honda goes
crazy the moment he hears "Ibu."

90
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:33,860
So you haven't told him about the thing yet?

91
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:37,880
We were only talking about the game, and look at this.
How could we possibly tell him anything?

92
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:42,800
Why would you talk about something
important while playing a game?

93
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:49,300
That's why I figured that if I casually mentioned Ibu going overseas while we were talking about the game,
it would hit him less hard.

94
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,080
Ibu is going overseas...

95
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:54,480
Ibu is going to a faraway place.

96
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,040
Thank you all for everything. Goodbye.

97
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,060
Overseas.

98
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,900
Ibu's going overseas

99
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,060
Hey, Honda

100
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:05,580
Honda-san

101
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:09,440
Ibu's going overseas

102
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,700
Ibu's going overseas

103
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,400
Are you okay, Honda?

104
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,840
Pull yourself together.

105
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,900
Ibu's going overseas

106
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:20,660
Stop it, seriously!
Ibu's really going overseas?

107
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:23,400
Oh no, the couple's going
to live in Africa together.

108
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,500
Africa

109
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,840
Listen carefully, Honda, and stay calm.

110
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,480
Ibu is going to Africa.

111
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:36,020
Deserts are spreading rapidly
all over the world right now.

112
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:38,880
They're even causing problems

113
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:42,920
and many people are being driven
from the land they lived on.

114
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:46,860
To stop desertification,
they need people doing hands-on work.

115
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,940
Kawasaki-kun once went to the Kalahari
Desert in Africa as a volunteer,

116
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:56,120
and he felt this was the work
worthy of staking his life on.

117
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,400
So he decided to head to
Africa after graduating.

118
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,420
As expected of the man Ibu-chan chose.

119
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,600
He has truly solid convictions.

120
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:07,820
Still, did he really have
to take Eve along too?

121
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:14,500
Eve has to stay where
I can keep an eye on her!

122
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:16,100
Please, senpai!

123
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:19,000
Please do something to keep
Eve from going to Africa!

124
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:23,580
Hello.

125
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:26,680
Welcome.

126
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,360
It's the first time you've come to our home,

127
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:32,280
it's a small place, but please come in.

128
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,400
Ryo-san.

129
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,540
About that matter, did you tell my brother?

130
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:40,980
I already told him.

131
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,840
He was a little surprised,
but he understood.

132
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,880
I see.

133
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:47,960
So, I've got something I want
to consult you about today.

134
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,120
Me, at Ibu-chan's house?

135
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,680
Yeah, until we leave for Africa,

136
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,040
we'd really like you to work there.

137
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:57,660
Why all of a sudden?

138
00:06:57,900 --> 00:07:02,040
Well, when we told Honda's
family about the Africa plan,

139
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,440
did they oppose it?

140
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:06,660
No, they all strongly agreed,
saying it's a admirable idea.

141
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:07,780
I see.

142
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:13,060
But Ibu's father started saying he'll miss her,
since he won't be able to see her anymore.

143
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:18,920
So we ended up suggesting that they live
together at the shop until they leave for Africa.

144
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:19,740
I see.

145
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:25,300
Didn't you two say you're both working part-time at a
convenience store to earn money for the trip to Africa?

146
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:26,000
Yes.

147
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:30,380
But between the apartment rent and living expenses,
we just can't save up.

148
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:32,720
Then this is all the more convenient,
isn't it?

149
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:37,340
Besides, Kawasaki-kun already loves motorcycles,
and he has a mechanic's license, right?

150
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,855
Yes. If that's the case,

151
00:07:39,905 --> 00:07:42,300
we'd really like that too, you know.

152
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:43,760
Yes.

153
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:47,940
Alright, then it's settled.
Good for you, Onjura!

154
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:49,340
Yes.

155
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,320
And this is a favor I have to ask.

156
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:57,880
While you two are at home,
forget all about going to Africa,

157
00:07:57,930 --> 00:08:01,600
the Honda family wants you
to enjoy your days together.

158
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:07,240
Could you please not mention going to Africa at all?
How about it?

159
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,280
Yes, understood.

160
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:11,160
Hello.

161
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:13,080
Hey, Ryo-san.

162
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,920
Long time no see

163
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:16,320
What brings you here today?

164
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,560
Actually, we have something to talk about.

165
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,260
What? Kawasaki-kun wants
to work at our place?

166
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,080
He says he really wants to work here.

167
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,600
But why all of a sudden?

168
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:31,580
Well, the other day I was talking with Kawasaki-kun,
and the subject of this shop came up.

169
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:37,054
He says he wants to keep riding,
so he's taking over the police work, and...

170
00:08:37,104 --> 00:08:39,140
My little brother Monkey hates motorcycles.

171
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:43,300
I told him that if things stayed like this,
nobody would take over Honda's bike shop.

172
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:44,540
And?

173
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,596
Then that Kawasaki guy,

174
00:08:46,646 --> 00:08:49,340
said he wanted to take it over himself.

175
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:51,640
Really?

176
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,600
Yeah. Apparently he's been
interested in bike shops for a while.

177
00:08:57,320 --> 00:09:00,560
That guy, that's exactly what we wanted.

178
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:03,440
Well then, it's settled.

179
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,020
That's great, I'm...

180
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,132
But, Dad,

181
00:09:08,182 --> 00:09:11,040
I have one request about that.

182
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:15,180
Kawasaki doesn't want to be coddled.

183
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:17,760
He wants you to train him hard.

184
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:21,840
So, Dad,
don't think of Kawasaki as your successor.

185
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,900
Just treat him like a part-timer
and be strict with him.

186
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:27,900
Whatever you do, don't say anything like
"you'll take over the shop,"

187
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,580
or you'll make him complacent.

188
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,160
Got it. Leave it to me.

189
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:35,220
Great success, great success!

190
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:38,920
But, senpai, will this really work out?

191
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:43,300
Anyway, as long as the two of them work together,
it'll be fine.

192
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:47,580
Listen, think about what
would happen if we did that.

193
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:48,800
What would happen?

194
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:57,000
Kawasaki watches his father work diligently every day,
watching, watching,

195
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:01,300
but Honda Forestry will close
with just the old man running it.

196
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,720
Kawasaki, who loves bikes,
must find it painful to watch.

197
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:11,140
So we'll pick the right moment and persuade
Kawasaki to take over the bike shop.

198
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:15,320
For Kawasaki, he can make a living doing what he loves,
working with bikes for life.

199
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,900
Even if he can't go to Africa,
he won't have any real complaints.

200
00:10:17,900 --> 00:10:20,820
Your father's satisfied too,
now that he has a successor.

201
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:23,180
And you're satisfied that
Ibu-chan isn't going far away.

202
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:25,580
Kawasaki's satisfied too,
now that he gets to run a bike shop.

203
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:27,440
Everyone's satisfied!

204
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,360
How about that, Honda? Perfect, isn't it!

205
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:31,560
Yeah, that's good!

206
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:35,440
I'm inexperienced,
but I look forward to working with you.

207
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,300
First, change the oil
on that bike over there.

208
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:39,620
Yes.

209
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:48,620
Hey, Car-sex-kun,
how long does an oil change take?

210
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:52,260
Sorry, the oil change itself is done,

211
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:54,600
but the brake system seems to be loose,

212
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,340
so I was checking it while I was at it.

213
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:59,020
So you noticed that.

214
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,820
I was planning to do it later myself.

215
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:05,420
I'll take care of this much on my end.

216
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,980
Impressive. At this rate,
you'll show us what you've got.

217
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,100
No, no, no!

218
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:10,960
Show it.

219
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,540
No, no, show, show, show!

220
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:14,620
You want to see it, don't you, old man?

221
00:11:14,620 --> 00:11:17,220
Yeah, the chichikuri mambo
is really Yato's specialty.

222
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:19,680
Dad, you're so into it.

223
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,180
Chichikuri mambo, chichikuri mambo!

224
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:23,820
Chichikuri mambo, and cue!

225
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:27,920
You really are a funny guy, aren't you?

226
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,040
Really? I'm funny?

227
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,000
Stop it, you're making me blush.

228
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,660
I told you, you can't just go
off and open a shop like that!

229
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:37,580
I see.

230
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:41,360
Kawasaki,
Ibu's cooking dinner tonight, right?

231
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,660
Has she gotten any better at cooking?

232
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:46,220
Yes, you can look forward to it.

233
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:49,880
When it comes to Ibu,
she can cook any ingredient well.

234
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:50,860
Even if she goes to Af-

235
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:52,760
Af?

236
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:54,485
No, that, Af, Af,

237
00:11:54,535 --> 00:11:57,260
You're a fan of Afro Namie,
aren't you, Kawasaki?

238
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,020
Yeah, yeah, Afro Namie, Afro Namie.

239
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:00,980
That's it.

240
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:05,360
I told you, you can't say you're going to Africa!
Laugh, laugh.

241
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,080
Let's eat!

242
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:14,100
We're pretty good, aren't we?

243
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:18,120
This is delicious, Ibu.
You've really improved.

244
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:18,740
Really?

245
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:22,260
It's nice to have a meal together like this,
isn't it.

246
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:24,660
This is how it should be.

247
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,820
By the way, Ryo-san,
about this part-time job...

248
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:30,020
Part-time job?

249
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,900
No, no, not that. I meant baritone.

250
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:34,680
Baritone's a good one.

251
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:37,160
A vacation on a southern island

252
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,980
I'm not interested.

253
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:40,240
Is that so?

254
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:44,200
Never mind that.
More importantly, Kawasaki-kun,

255
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,860
I'm really happy, you know.

256
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:47,760
this way, you'll take over for me.

257
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:50,780
Right away?

258
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,600
No, that's not what I meant.
I mean, right away...

259
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:53,740
Right away, right away, bash!

260
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,340
Dear!

261
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:57,560
Dear!

262
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,080
Dear!

263
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:02,860
Is it really going to be okay like that?

264
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,680
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

265
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,720
No thanks, sorry, I'm already full.

266
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:34,320
Things are looking good

267
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:36,400
At this rate, it should be fine.

268
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:39,540
Kawasaki's joining Honda's motorcycle shop?

269
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:42,220
Yeah, it's only a matter of
time before he gets a job.

270
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:44,480
What's going to happen with the Africa trip?

271
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:45,880
Isn't he going to quit?

272
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,480
No way.

273
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:48,540
It'll be fine, Kei-chan.

274
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:51,520
There's no way the plan will work out.

275
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,480
Right?

276
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,540
You can say whatever you want.

277
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:57,420
It's bad, everything's gotten out!

278
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:58,880
What?

279
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:00,800
I knew it.

280
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:02,740
What are we supposed to do now?

281
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:04,000
Senpai.

282
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:07,140
What on earth happened, Honda?

283
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:09,400
Well, that's...

284
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,360
Lift it up a little there.

285
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,140
Like this?

286
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:14,500
Just like that.

287
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:23,840
Jess

288
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:26,120
Long time no see.

289
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:28,160
You bastards are still alive

290
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:29,740
That's harsh, Oyasan.

291
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:34,400
The other day we blasted nonstop all the way to Kagoshima,
you know.

292
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:37,260
What, you're still doing that stupid stuff?

293
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:38,100
Tch.

294
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:45,840
What, ban those guys from earlier?
Is that what you're saying?

295
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:46,280
Yes.

296
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,360
What kind of charge is this?

297
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,700
If word gets out that this
is a shop where men hang out,

298
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:54,320
this shop will also be
looked at with suspicion.

299
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:57,220
Ordinary customers won't want to come in.

300
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:59,480
That's a request I can't agree to.

301
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:00,900
Dad.

302
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:03,200
I choose who my customers are.

303
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,120
This is how Honda Forestry does things.

304
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,380
If you plan to take over the shop,
you'd better remember that.

305
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,780
Take over the shop?
What are you talking about?

306
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:14,380
Ibu and I plan to go to Africa once
we've saved up our part-time pay.

307
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,800
I have no intention of
taking over this shop.

308
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:18,940
What?!

309
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:23,200
Big brother,
is it really all right with Kimuchu?

310
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:24,420
It's fine, it's fine.

311
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:26,860
Did you deceive me, you bastard?

312
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:28,340
You're the one who deceived me, aren't you?

313
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,660
How can you be so brazen
after what you've done?

314
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:33,340
I never heard anything
about taking over the shop.

315
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:36,360
I didn't hear anything about going to Africa either,
you know!

316
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,540
Stop it, both of you!

317
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:41,720
Dad, Zephyr-san,
why would you do something like this?

318
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:48,560
Excuse me.

319
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:51,820
Chepa-san.

320
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,560
Chepa.

321
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:57,600
Kawasaki-kun never came back after that.

322
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:01,120
If we don't bring him back,
Ibu says she'll break up with me.

323
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,100
Senpai.

324
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,940
Please do something about it.

325
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:05,520
What are we going to do, Senpai?

326
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:07,940
It's all Ryo-chan's fault, you know.

327
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:17,660
Found you.

328
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:21,260
Ryo-san, big brother.

329
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:23,440
Sorry for deceiving you like that.

330
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,940
I'm the one who set up all of that.

331
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:28,300
No, I'm the one who forced it.

332
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,100
That's all in the past now.

333
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,900
Am I just too rigid?

334
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,980
I just can't forgive bōsōzoku,
no matter what.

335
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:44,180
Can't you trust that old man?

336
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:48,100
Even I used to think people could understand
each other if they just talked it out.

337
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:51,040
I don't exactly trust him,

338
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,000
but still,

339
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,080
that old man is the real deal.

340
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:56,480
The people he associates with

341
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:59,340
aren't really such bad people, I think.

342
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:01,480
So what do you say?

343
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:03,120
Why don't you

344
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:04,600
really get to know that old man?

345
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:07,760
Then you might start to see something.

346
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,200
Yesterday,

347
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,360
please let me work here once more.

348
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:38,640
Is this the motorcycle?

349
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,300
Yes.

350
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:41,960
Can it be fixed?

351
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:44,680
A Kawasaki A1 Samurai

352
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:48,340
There aren't any parts left for it.

353
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:50,100
It's shot.

354
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,820
Isn't this bike your own, by any chance?

355
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:54,480
Yes.

356
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,580
It's my husband's keepsake.

357
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:01,540
My husband loved motorcycles
since he was young.

358
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:04,600
But exactly twenty years ago,

359
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:07,840
on a mountain road at night,
he couldn't make it through a sharp curve.

360
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:10,520
He had just heard that our
child was about to be born.

361
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:11,960
He must have been in a great hurry.

362
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:15,380
He left without ever
seeing this child's face.

363
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:19,420
It was precious to my husband,
so I couldn't bring myself to throw it away.

364
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:20,520
I see.

365
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:26,260
I... I always hated the motorcycle
that took my father's life.

366
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,400
I begged Mom again and again to
get rid of this motorcycle, too.

367
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,780
But recently, I suddenly started to wonder.

368
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,600
Are motorcycles really that wonderful?

369
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:40,400
What was it about motorcycles
that drew Dad in so much?

370
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:44,700
And then somehow,
I felt like riding one myself.

371
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:46,500
So I got my motorcycle license.

372
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:49,240
I decided to ride the motorcycle Dad loved.

373
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,380
Through the motorcycle,

374
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,860
I think I wanted to feel close to Dad.

375
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:55,840
If that could be arranged,

376
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:58,280
I was wondering if she could ride
the bike her father used to ride.

377
00:18:59,020 --> 00:18:59,680
I see.

378
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:01,380
What do you think?

379
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:04,420
Could you indulge my daughter's wish?

380
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:05,280
Please.

381
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:08,140
Don't worry.

382
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:09,960
We'll make it work somehow.

383
00:19:10,660 --> 00:19:11,380
You.

384
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:12,800
Thank you in advance.

385
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:13,840
Please.

386
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:16,880
Understood.

387
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:18,460
Thank you very much.

388
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:21,580
I'm leaving this one to you, got it?

389
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,180
Make sure you take good care of it.

390
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:24,280
Yes.

391
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,120
Are you alright on your own?

392
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:33,660
Yes.

393
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,020
Sorry.

394
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:36,980
Taking on such a troublesome repair...

395
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:38,940
Tell me about it.

396
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:41,200
But no matter what,

397
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,340
I want to let that girl ride this bike.

398
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,440
That's what I thought.

399
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:48,660
You're naive.
Work is a lot harsher than that.

400
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:51,440
Sometimes feelings alone aren't
enough to get things done.

401
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:58,540
But I think it's also important
to cherish feelings like that.

402
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:02,920
If you hadn't spoken up back then,
I would've taken it on myself.

403
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,080
Dad.

404
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:12,540
Those two make a pretty good pair,
don't they?

405
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:13,320
I'm glad.

406
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:29,820
So, how's it running?

407
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:32,720
Yes, it's mostly fixed,

408
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:35,780
but this carburetor is completely useless.

409
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:37,180
So it's what I thought.

410
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,700
We checked with manufacturers,
secondhand shops,

411
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:41,140
and everywhere else we could think of,

412
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:42,420
but there's nowhere left

413
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:44,200
I see.

414
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:46,220
If only we could somehow make it work...

415
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:56,260
Good night.

416
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,620
We found it.

417
00:20:58,140 --> 00:20:59,340
The carburetor for the A1.

418
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:02,540
So you found it. Well done.

419
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,040
It was pretty hard, you know.

420
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:08,800
We split up and searched all over the place.

421
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:10,620
But, you know,

422
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:14,020
it was the old man's request,
so we couldn't just refuse.

423
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:15,880
That's how it goes, isn't it.

424
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:16,900
You idiot!

425
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:19,360
Here you go.

426
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:20,480
Yes.

427
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:27,500
Thank you all so much.

428
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:30,040
N-no, we didn't do anything that big.

429
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:32,320
That's right,
you didn't do anything, did you?

430
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:33,300
That's harsh.

431
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:48,520
Alright, go on.

432
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:49,400
Yes.

433
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:53,640
Yay!

434
00:22:03,660 --> 00:22:04,460
Father.

435
00:22:05,340 --> 00:22:07,920
So this is the view Dad used to see.

436
00:22:13,060 --> 00:22:15,040
Let's just go touring like this.

437
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:15,900
Yes.

438
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:17,300
Go, Honda!

439
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,340
Here we go.

440
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:40,280
Dad, riding bikes is wonderful, isn't it?

441
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:42,540
So you finally get it?

442
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:44,320
Please.

443
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:46,880
Let me take over that shop.

444
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:50,780
You.

445
00:22:52,660 --> 00:22:54,940
No! You're going to Africa, aren't you?

446
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:57,660
A man doesn't go back on
what he's decided once!

447
00:22:57,780 --> 00:22:59,920
Bikes over Africa! I've made up my mind!

448
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:00,960
No way, no way!

449
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:06,440
Everyone at the police box,

450
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:09,040
thank you for all your help back then.

451
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:13,720
Eve and I are now working
as volunteers in Africa,

452
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:15,040
and we run a motorcycle shop.

453
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:19,780
We're working hard every day to live up to
the name of Honda Forestry's Africa branch.

454
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:24,680
I know I've left you feeling lonely,
big brother,

455
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:28,020
but Eve is doing well too,
so please tell everyone not to worry.

456
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:32,320
But elephants sometimes come by the shop,
which is a bit of a problem.

457
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:33,020
Elephant?

458
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,000
What's this?

459
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:37,340
Look, look, look!

460
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:39,840
Chintoro, don't you dare run off!

461
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:40,200
Wow!

462
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:14,060
I crumpled up boredom like a
reprimand and tossed it away.

463
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:17,500
Naked instincts, bare instincts.

464
00:24:17,500 --> 00:24:18,560
Playing the fool,

465
00:24:19,420 --> 00:24:22,340
reckless and broke, so what?

466
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:28,140
It's my way, I'll just do what I want.

467
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:32,660
The stern Chief's thunder,
smoke from his head.

468
00:24:33,500 --> 00:24:35,960
Run away, and they'll put up a wall.

469
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:37,460
Well, that's something to celebrate.

470
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:38,300
Ohhh!

471
00:24:38,300 --> 00:24:39,900
To flowering Edo,

472
00:24:39,900 --> 00:24:40,400
Just a sec,

473
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:41,920
Ryōzan taifū

474
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,900
Always

475
00:24:42,900 --> 00:24:45,460
Howling winds

476
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:47,420
Atarakamo purei kyūraito

477
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:49,100
Jugemu jugemu

478
00:24:49,100 --> 00:24:50,280
Kokono suigire

479
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,380
Taishitari suigyo

480
00:24:51,380 --> 00:24:53,120
Suigyo batsukun

481
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:54,060
Gyo batsukun

482
00:24:54,060 --> 00:24:54,880
Raibatsukun

483
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:56,460
Neru tokoro ni sumu tokoro

484
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,140
Yabura kōji

485
00:24:58,140 --> 00:24:58,860
Bura kōji

486
00:24:58,860 --> 00:25:00,120
Paipo paipo paipo

487
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,200
Shūringan

488
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,140
Shūringan no gūrindai

489
00:25:03,140 --> 00:25:04,900
Gūrindai no ponpoko

490
00:25:04,900 --> 00:25:06,340
Hīrō ponpokonā no

491
00:25:15,420 --> 00:25:16,740
What the hell is going on?

492
00:25:16,740 --> 00:25:19,000
Lemon stopped eating rice.

493
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:21,480
"I'll get fat,
so I don't want to eat anymore," he says?

494
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,420
What is this kindergartener talking about?

495
00:25:23,420 --> 00:25:25,340
Lemon, basically, with that kind of thing,

496
00:25:25,340 --> 00:25:26,800
you're completely relying
on those beneath you.

497
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:28,840
What's going to happen to
the super-sensitive master?

498
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:31,020
Next time: Lemon's strike.

499
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:32,120
Nice to meet you.

500
00:25:37,460 --> 00:25:39,080
Surely there's a wall.

501
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:44,280
Everyone, come to our town!

502
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:45,920
Thank you.

